%"], "rationale": "Polls, raters, markets and Ossoff's overwhelming fundraising edge all point the same direction, supporting a high-single-digit Democratic margin. A slight trim from the polling average accounts for Republican-leaning pollsters' recent tighter numbers and the usual uncertainty in a midterm environment.", "watch": "A late shift in the national midterm environment or a tightening governor's race dragging turnout could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Jon Ossoff seeks a second term against Trump-endorsed Rep. Mike Collins, who emerged from a contested Republican runoff. Georgia remains a narrowly Republican-leaning state overall, but Ossoff has built a durable position through strong name recognition and record fundraising.\n\nEvery recent poll shows Ossoff ahead, with margins ranging from four to eleven points and an average near eight or nine. He holds a cash advantage of more than $40 million, and outside groups have spent little on either side so far. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Ossoff's chances above 90 percent. Headlines suggest national Republicans see the seat slipping away, though a tight governor's race could complicate turnout dynamics.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9522, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9495, "margin": 8.5}]}